On Tue, 12 May 2009 17:25:30 +0200, Link <chillynois@yahoo.com> wrote:

> In SLASHEM, what exactly does TECHLEVEL mean?  Is it another word for
> "character level"?

No, it's the level of the technique.

At certain (character) level, you gain techniques that you can use  
afterwards (invoking the right menu). The technique starts at level 1 and  
gain one TECHLEVEL each time you gain another (character) level. The  
efficiency of the technique depends on the TECHLEVEL.

The notion is (somewhat) useful because some techniques are gained by  
several classes at different levels, so for a given character level, the  
TECHLEVEL might change...

